Subject: [PATCH 11/12] =?UTF-8?q?Big=20screen=20transitions:=203=E2=80=934?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=C3=97=20smoother=20(GPU-only=20movement,=20cheaper=20lobby)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the projector page (1920×1080, software compositing): every
entrance ran at 1–6 fps with single frames up to ~1 s. The main thread was
nearly idle; the time went to re-rasterising and compositing the screen on
every frame. Causes, each fixed and re-measured:

- clip-path reveals repainted the whole incoming screen every frame
  → rolls are now the screen itself coming down/up (transform), the roller
    bar rides on a transform (was `top`, layout per frame); curtain is two
    velvet stage curtains parting over the new picture; iris is a cover with
    a growing opening (only the cover repaints, never the content)
- the lobby aurora: three gradients under a live 70px blur + blend mode,
  re-blurred on every frame → softness built into the gradients, no filter,
  no blend; drift stays transform-only (screenshots: same look)
- the lobby grid's full-screen CSS mask → drawn once into an image at the
  screen's size (pixel-identical), plain background from then on
- the closed operator panel stayed a live backdrop-blurred layer above the
  screen → visibility:hidden once it has slid away (also: not tabbable)
- shorter: rolls 1000→700 ms, curtain 850→700, iris 900→650, slide 700→550,
  zoom 650→450, flip 850→650

Same machine, same settings, deck in / lobby back:
  roll down 3/6 → 13/18 fps · curtain 3/6 → 14/14 · zoom 4/5 → 12/14
  (worst roll-down frame 408 → 103 ms). None / Fade unchanged.
